# vanpi: keep the disk hub chain off USB 2.0 (the fast path).
#
# Installed as /etc/udev/rules.d/70-vanpi-usb2-disk-hub-off.rules (root:root, 0644).
# Contract and procedure: docs/agent-context.md, section "USB 2.0 block for the disk hub chain".
#
# The Pi 4's onboard hub (VIA 2109:3431, always USB path 1-1) carries the CAN adapters' hub on
# port 4. Port 2 is the USB 2.0 half of the external disk hub chain, whose disks all run on
# USB 3.0 (bus 2). Faults in that chain are the suspected cause of the whole onboard USB 2.0 hub
# failing, CAN adapters included, so port 2 is powered off as soon as the onboard hub's driver is
# bound: at boot (udev's coldplug "add") and after a re-bind of the hub ("bind").
#
# This write happens once per event and udev ignores its failure. The watcher
# (vanpi-usb2-disk-hub-off.service) verifies that the block holds, retries and alerts.
#
# TEST skips the hot-plug "add", where the hub driver has not created its ports yet.
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", KERNEL=="1-1:1.0", ATTRS{idVendor}=="2109", ATTRS{idProduct}=="3431", TEST=="1-1-port2/disable", ATTR{1-1-port2/disable}="1"
